IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `la-dates`

-- Limitation Act 1969 (NSW) -- the rules a person bringing a claim for damages meets: no limitation period for child
-- abuse (s 6A, with Schedule 5 Part 3 for claims already barred or judged), the personal injury periods (Part 2
-- Division 6, ss 50A-50F; and s 18A, s 19 for an act or omission before Division 6 began), the general periods for
-- other money claims (ss 14, 16, 17, 18), the ultimate bar (s 51), disability (s 52), fraud and concealment (s 55),
-- the court's extensions for a personal injury claim (Part 3 Division 4, ss 62A, 62D, 62F), and what expiry does to the
-- right (s 63).
--
-- This module holds the law. The questions are asked in la-seat.l4 (the person bringing the claim), which IMPORTs it
-- and restates no rule. Nothing here is exported.
--
-- ANSWERS are named outcomes (enumerations), dates or numbers, never MAYBE BOOLEAN, so no NOTHING-kind tag is used.
-- Where the text says no in its own words (a "means" definition, "only if", "does not apply", "nothing in this Act")
-- the outcome begins "no:"; where it does not answer, the outcome says "the Act does not say"; where a provision's
-- scope (without "only") is not met, the outcome says the provision "does not reach this". Judgments the Act leaves to
-- the court ("just and reasonable", "irrational decision", "knows or ought to know", "reasonable diligence") are
-- inputs: the answer is conditional on them, never a guess at them.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website at 10 March 2025, via the Open Australian
-- Legal Corpus (version as at 16 June 2022). State of New South Wales, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE
-- ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Limitation Act 1969`

§§ `Days the Act turns on`

-- s 18A(1)(b), s 19(1), s 57A: 1 September 1990, the commencement of the Limitation (Amendment) Act 1990 (named in the
-- text itself).
`1 September 1990` MEANS `the date` 1 9 1990
-- s 50A(2): Division 6 applies only where the act or omission "occurs on or after the commencement of this Division (as
-- inserted by the Civil Liability Amendment (Personal Responsibility) Act 2002)". The deposited text does not give the
-- day; 6 December 2002 is taken from that Act's commencement (finding 1 in NOTES.md: not from the deposit).
`the day Division 6 commenced` MEANS `the date` 6 12 2002

§§ `Part 1, s 6A -- no limitation period for child abuse actions`

-- s 6A(2): "child abuse means any of the following perpetrated against a person when the person is under 18 years of
-- age -- (a) sexual abuse, (b) serious physical abuse, (c) any other abuse (connected abuse) perpetrated in connection
-- with sexual abuse or serious physical abuse of the person (whether or not the connected abuse was perpetrated by the
-- person who perpetrated the sexual abuse or serious physical abuse)." s 6A(3): "connected abuse is child abuse only if
-- both the connected abuse and the sexual abuse or serious physical abuse in connection with which it is perpetrated
-- are perpetrated when the person is under 18 years of age." A "means" list: a kind not in it is not child abuse.
DECLARE `Kind of abuse` IS ONE OF
    `sexual abuse`
    `serious physical abuse`
    `other abuse connected with sexual or serious physical abuse of me, which was also perpetrated before I turned 18`
    `other abuse connected with sexual or serious physical abuse of me, which was perpetrated when I was 18 or older`
    `physical abuse that was not serious, not connected with sexual or serious physical abuse`
    `other abuse not connected with sexual or serious physical abuse`
    `the injury did not result from abuse`

DECLARE `Child abuse answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes, no time limit: an action for damages for death or personal injury resulting from child abuse may be brought at any time and is not subject to any limitation period under this Act (s 6A(1)); the court keeps its powers, for example to dismiss or stay proceedings where a fair trial is no longer possible (s 6A(6))`
    `no: child abuse is abuse perpetrated against you when you were under 18 years of age (s 6A(2)), and this abuse was not`
    `no: connected abuse is child abuse only if the sexual or serious physical abuse it was connected with was also perpetrated when you were under 18 (s 6A(3))`
    `no: child abuse means sexual abuse, serious physical abuse, or other abuse connected with either (s 6A(2)), and this abuse is none of them`
    `no: s 6A applies only to damages for death or personal injury resulting from child abuse, and this injury did not result from abuse (s 6A(1))`
    `no: s 6A covers only an action for damages that relates to death or personal injury (s 6A(1))`

GIVEN `the day of birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the 18th birthday after` `the day of birth` MEANS `the day of birth` `plus months` 216

GIVEN `the day of birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the 25th birthday after` `the day of birth` MEANS `the day of birth` `plus months` 300

-- s 6A(1): "An action for damages that relates to the death of or personal injury to a person resulting from an act or
-- omission that constitutes child abuse of the person may be brought at any time and is not subject to any limitation
-- period under this Act despite any other provision of this Act." s 6A(4), (5): however the claim is brought (tort,
-- contract, statute), and for the relatives (Compensation to Relatives Act 1897) or the estate (survivor action). The
-- day of the abuse is the day it (or the first of it) was perpetrated (fork F3).
GIVEN `the kind of abuse` IS A `Kind of abuse`
      `the claim is for damages for death or personal injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injured person's date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the day the abuse was perpetrated` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Child abuse answer`
`the s 6A answer for` `the kind of abuse` `with a personal injury claim` `the claim is for damages for death or personal injury` `born` `the injured person's date of birth` `abused on` `the day the abuse was perpetrated` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the claim is for damages for death or personal injury`
        THEN `no: s 6A covers only an action for damages that relates to death or personal injury (s 6A(1))`
        IF `the kind of abuse` EQUALS `the injury did not result from abuse`
        THEN `no: s 6A applies only to damages for death or personal injury resulting from child abuse, and this injury did not result from abuse (s 6A(1))`
        IF     `the kind of abuse` EQUALS `physical abuse that was not serious, not connected with sexual or serious physical abuse`
            OR `the kind of abuse` EQUALS `other abuse not connected with sexual or serious physical abuse`
        THEN `no: child abuse means sexual abuse, serious physical abuse, or other abuse connected with either (s 6A(2)), and this abuse is none of them`
        IF NOT (`the day the abuse was perpetrated` `is before` (`the 18th birthday after` `the injured person's date of birth`))
        THEN `no: child abuse is abuse perpetrated against you when you were under 18 years of age (s 6A(2)), and this abuse was not`
        IF `the kind of abuse` EQUALS `other abuse connected with sexual or serious physical abuse of me, which was perpetrated when I was 18 or older`
        THEN `no: connected abuse is child abuse only if the sexual or serious physical abuse it was connected with was also perpetrated when you were under 18 (s 6A(3))`
        OTHERWISE `yes, no time limit: an action for damages for death or personal injury resulting from child abuse may be brought at any time and is not subject to any limitation period under this Act (s 6A(1)); the court keeps its powers, for example to dismiss or stay proceedings where a fair trial is no longer possible (s 6A(6))`

GIVEN `the answer` IS A `Child abuse answer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 6A applies on` `the answer` IF
    `the answer` EQUALS `yes, no time limit: an action for damages for death or personal injury resulting from child abuse may be brought at any time and is not subject to any limitation period under this Act (s 6A(1)); the court keeps its powers, for example to dismiss or stay proceedings where a fair trial is no longer possible (s 6A(6))`

§§ `Schedule 5 Part 3 -- claims barred or judged before s 6A`

-- Sch 5 cl 9: s 6A "extends to a cause of action that arose before the commencement of that section, and applies -- (a)
-- whether or not any limitation period previously applying to the cause of action has expired, and (b) whether or not
-- an action has been commenced previously on the cause of action, and (c) whether or not a judgment on the cause of
-- action has, on the ground that a limitation period applying to the cause of action had expired, been given
-- previously, and (d) whether or not a judgment in respect of legal professional negligence has, on [that] ground ...
-- been given previously." cl 10(1), (2): such an action "may be brought ... as if the action in which such a judgment
-- was given had not itself been commenced"; cl 10(3): the court hearing it "may, if it decides that it is just and
-- reasonable to do so", set aside the judgment and take into account damages and costs paid or payable under it;
-- cl 10(4), (5): the Supreme Court may set aside a judgment even though not hearing the action; another court may not
-- set aside a judgment of any other court. cl 8(2): "a reference to a judgment given extends to a judgment entered and
-- also to an agreement entered into before and in connection with any such judgment."
DECLARE `Earlier proceedings` IS ONE OF
    `there was no earlier action or judgment on the claim`
    `an earlier action was commenced, but no judgment was given on the ground that the limitation period had expired`
    `a judgment on the claim was given or entered on the ground that the limitation period had expired`
    `a judgment against my lawyers for professional negligence was given on the ground that a limitation period had expired`
    `an agreement was made before and in connection with such a judgment`
    `the claim was settled, with no judgment on the limitation ground`

DECLARE `Previously barred answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: s 6A applies to a cause of action that arose before s 6A commenced, whether or not a limitation period had already expired (Sch 5 cl 9(a))`
    `yes: s 6A applies whether or not an action was commenced previously on the claim (Sch 5 cl 9(b))`
    `yes: you may bring the action as if the earlier action had not been commenced; the court hearing it may, if it decides it is just and reasonable, set aside the earlier judgment and take into account damages and costs paid or payable under it (Sch 5 cll 8(2), 9, 10); only the Supreme Court may set aside another court's judgment`
    `the Act does not say: Schedule 5 deals with judgments and with agreements made in connection with a judgment (cl 8(2)), not with a settlement made without one`
    `no: s 6A does not apply to the claim on these facts, so Schedule 5 Part 3 does not help`

GIVEN `the s 6A answer` IS A `Child abuse answer`
      `the earlier proceedings` IS AN `Earlier proceedings`
GIVETH A `Previously barred answer`
`the Schedule 5 answer for` `the s 6A answer` `after` `the earlier proceedings` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 6A applies on` `the s 6A answer`)
    THEN `no: s 6A does not apply to the claim on these facts, so Schedule 5 Part 3 does not help`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the earlier proceedings`
         WHEN `there was no earlier action or judgment on the claim` THEN `yes: s 6A applies to a cause of action that arose before s 6A commenced, whether or not a limitation period had already expired (Sch 5 cl 9(a))`
         WHEN `an earlier action was commenced, but no judgment was given on the ground that the limitation period had expired` THEN `yes: s 6A applies whether or not an action was commenced previously on the claim (Sch 5 cl 9(b))`
         WHEN `the claim was settled, with no judgment on the limitation ground` THEN `the Act does not say: Schedule 5 deals with judgments and with agreements made in connection with a judgment (cl 8(2)), not with a settlement made without one`
         OTHERWISE `yes: you may bring the action as if the earlier action had not been commenced; the court hearing it may, if it decides it is just and reasonable, set aside the earlier judgment and take into account damages and costs paid or payable under it (Sch 5 cll 8(2), 9, 10); only the Supreme Court may set aside another court's judgment`

§§ `The claim, and which period applies (Part 2)`

-- One claim, by one plaintiff, against one defendant. s 11(1): "Personal injury includes any disease and any
-- impairment of the physical or mental condition of a person." s 50A(1): Division 6 applies "regardless of whether the
-- claim for the damages is brought in tort, in contract, under statute or otherwise".
DECLARE `Kind of claim` IS ONE OF
    `damages for death or personal injury`
    `damages or money in contract (not under a deed) or tort with no personal injury, or money recoverable under an enactment`
    `a claim founded on a deed`
    `a claim on a judgment`
    `a penalty or forfeiture recoverable under an enactment`
    `a claim for which another Act fixes the limitation period, such as a motor accident claim`
    `another kind of claim`

-- s 50B: "survivor action means a cause of action that survives on the death of a person for the benefit of the
-- person's estate under section 2 of the Law Reform (Miscellaneous Provisions) Act 1944"; "compensation to relatives
-- action means a cause of action that arises under the Compensation to Relatives Act 1897".
DECLARE `Plaintiff` IS ONE OF
    `the person injured or wronged, suing for themselves`
    `the personal representative of the injured person, who has died, suing for the estate (a survivor action)`
    `relatives suing for the death (a compensation to relatives action)`

DECLARE `Claim facts` HAS
    `the kind of claim` IS A `Kind of claim`
    `the plaintiff` IS A `Plaintiff`
    `the kind of abuse` IS A `Kind of abuse`
    `the day of the act or omission` IS A DATE
    `the injured person's date of birth` IS A DATE
    `the day the cause of action accrued` IS A DATE
    `the day the claim became discoverable by the plaintiff` IS A DATE
    `the defendant was a parent or guardian of the injured person, or a close associate of one` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the injured person had a capable parent or guardian while a minor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the injured person was incapacitated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the incapacity began` IS A DATE
    `the incapacity has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the incapacity ended` IS A DATE
    `the injured person was a protected person while incapacitated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day of the death` IS A DATE
    `the deceased could discover the claim before the death` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the claim became discoverable by the deceased` IS A DATE
    `the day the personal representative was appointed` IS A DATE
    `there was fraud, deceit or concealment by the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the fraud or concealment was or could have been discovered` IS A DATE

DECLARE `Period answer` IS ONE OF
    `none: an action for child abuse may be brought at any time (s 6A)`
    `the first to expire of 3 years running from and including the day the claim is discoverable, and 12 years running from the act or omission (s 50C(1))`
    `the first to expire of 3 years from the day the claim is discoverable, which is no earlier than the victim's 25th birthday, and 12 years running from that birthday (s 50C(1), s 50E)`
    `the first to expire of 3 years from the day the claim is discoverable, which is no earlier than the death, and 12 years running from the death (s 50C(1), (3), s 50D(4))`
    `the first to expire of 3 years from the day the claim is discoverable as s 50C(2) works it out for a survivor action, and 12 years running from the act or omission (s 50C(1), (2))`
    `3 years running from the day the cause of action accrued (s 18A)`
    `3 years running from the death (s 19(1)(b))`
    `6 years running from the death (s 19(1)(a))`
    `6 years running from the day the cause of action accrued (s 14)`
    `12 years running from the day the cause of action accrued (s 16)`
    `12 years running from the day the judgment became enforceable (s 17)`
    `2 years running from the day the cause of action accrued (s 18)`
    `no: nothing in this Act applies where another Act fixes the limitation period (s 7(a); for a motor accident claim also s 50A(3))`
    `not covered: a personal injury claim that accrued before 1 September 1990 (Part 3 Division 3 Subdivision 1)`
    `not covered: a kind of claim this encoding does not cover`

GIVEN f IS A `Claim facts`
GIVETH A `Child abuse answer`
`the s 6A answer on` f MEANS
    `the s 6A answer for` (f's `the kind of abuse`) `with a personal injury claim` (f's `the kind of claim` EQUALS `damages for death or personal injury`) `born` (f's `the injured person's date of birth`) `abused on` (f's `the day of the act or omission`)

-- s 50A(2): Division 6 "applies only to causes of action where the act or omission alleged to have resulted in the
-- injury or death ... occurs on or after the commencement of this Division". s 6A applies "despite any other provision".
GIVEN f IS A `Claim facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Division 6 applies to` f IF
        f's `the kind of claim` EQUALS `damages for death or personal injury`
    AND (NOT (`s 6A applies on` (`the s 6A answer on` f)))
    AND (`the day Division 6 commenced` `is on or before` (f's `the day of the act or omission`))

-- s 50E(1): "If a cause of action is founded on the death of or injury to a person (the victim) who was a minor at the
-- time of the act or omission ... and the cause of action is against a person who at that time was a parent or guardian
-- of the victim or a close associate of a parent or guardian of the victim". s 50E(2) defines "close associate" by the
-- influence or unwillingness it describes: asked as one fact.
GIVEN f IS A `Claim facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 50E applies to` f IF
        `Division 6 applies to` f
    AND ((f's `the day of the act or omission`) `is before` (`the 18th birthday after` (f's `the injured person's date of birth`)))
    AND f's `the defendant was a parent or guardian of the injured person, or a close associate of one`

GIVEN f IS A `Claim facts`
GIVETH A `Period answer`
`the period for` f MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF f's `the kind of claim` EQUALS `a claim for which another Act fixes the limitation period, such as a motor accident claim`
        THEN `no: nothing in this Act applies where another Act fixes the limitation period (s 7(a); for a motor accident claim also s 50A(3))`
        IF f's `the kind of claim` EQUALS `damages or money in contract (not under a deed) or tort with no personal injury, or money recoverable under an enactment`
        THEN `6 years running from the day the cause of action accrued (s 14)`
        IF f's `the kind of claim` EQUALS `a claim founded on a deed`
        THEN `12 years running from the day the cause of action accrued (s 16)`
        IF f's `the kind of claim` EQUALS `a claim on a judgment`
        THEN `12 years running from the day the judgment became enforceable (s 17)`
        IF f's `the kind of claim` EQUALS `a penalty or forfeiture recoverable under an enactment`
        THEN `2 years running from the day the cause of action accrued (s 18)`
        IF f's `the kind of claim` EQUALS `another kind of claim`
        THEN `not covered: a kind of claim this encoding does not cover`
        IF `s 6A applies on` (`the s 6A answer on` f)
        THEN `none: an action for child abuse may be brought at any time (s 6A)`
        IF `s 50E applies to` f
        THEN `the first to expire of 3 years from the day the claim is discoverable, which is no earlier than the victim's 25th birthday, and 12 years running from that birthday (s 50C(1), s 50E)`
        IF (`Division 6 applies to` f) AND (f's `the plaintiff` EQUALS `relatives suing for the death (a compensation to relatives action)`)
        THEN `the first to expire of 3 years from the day the claim is discoverable, which is no earlier than the death, and 12 years running from the death (s 50C(1), (3), s 50D(4))`
        IF (`Division 6 applies to` f) AND (f's `the plaintiff` EQUALS `the personal representative of the injured person, who has died, suing for the estate (a survivor action)`)
        THEN `the first to expire of 3 years from the day the claim is discoverable as s 50C(2) works it out for a survivor action, and 12 years running from the act or omission (s 50C(1), (2))`
        IF `Division 6 applies to` f
        THEN `the first to expire of 3 years running from and including the day the claim is discoverable, and 12 years running from the act or omission (s 50C(1))`
        -- Before Division 6: s 19 for the relatives, s 18A for the rest (s 18A(1)(b): not before 1 September 1990).
        IF     f's `the plaintiff` EQUALS `relatives suing for the death (a compensation to relatives action)`
           AND ((f's `the day of the death`) `is before` `1 September 1990`)
        THEN `6 years running from the death (s 19(1)(a))`
        IF f's `the plaintiff` EQUALS `relatives suing for the death (a compensation to relatives action)`
        THEN `3 years running from the death (s 19(1)(b))`
        IF (f's `the day the cause of action accrued`) `is before` `1 September 1990`
        THEN `not covered: a personal injury claim that accrued before 1 September 1990 (Part 3 Division 3 Subdivision 1)`
        OTHERWISE `3 years running from the day the cause of action accrued (s 18A)`

-- The length in months and the day the Part 2 period runs from, for the periods outside Division 6.
GIVEN `the period` IS A `Period answer`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the months in` `the period` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the period`
    WHEN `3 years running from the day the cause of action accrued (s 18A)` THEN 36
    WHEN `3 years running from the death (s 19(1)(b))` THEN 36
    WHEN `6 years running from the death (s 19(1)(a))` THEN 72
    WHEN `6 years running from the day the cause of action accrued (s 14)` THEN 72
    WHEN `12 years running from the day the cause of action accrued (s 16)` THEN 144
    WHEN `12 years running from the day the judgment became enforceable (s 17)` THEN 144
    WHEN `2 years running from the day the cause of action accrued (s 18)` THEN 24
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN f IS A `Claim facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the ordinary period runs from for` f MEANS
    IF f's `the plaintiff` EQUALS `relatives suing for the death (a compensation to relatives action)`
       AND f's `the kind of claim` EQUALS `damages for death or personal injury`
    THEN f's `the day of the death`
    ELSE f's `the day the cause of action accrued`

§§ `Division 6 -- discoverability and the two periods`

-- s 50D(1): discoverable "on the first date that the person knows or ought to know" that the injury or death occurred,
-- that it was caused by the fault of the defendant, and (for injury) that it was sufficiently serious to justify an
-- action; s 50D(2), (3) and s 50F(3) (a capable parent's knowledge counts for a minor) shape that judgment, which is
-- an input. s 50D(4): a compensation to relatives action "is not discoverable before the date of death".
-- s 50C(2), survivor action: the earliest of (a) the day discoverable by the deceased "if the cause of action is
-- discoverable by the deceased more than 3 years before the death", (b) the personal representative's appointment "if
-- the cause of action is discoverable by the plaintiff at or before the time of that appointment", (c) the day
-- discoverable by the plaintiff if after the appointment.
GIVEN f IS A `Claim facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the s 50C(2) day for` f MEANS
    IF     f's `the deceased could discover the claim before the death`
       AND (((f's `the day the claim became discoverable by the deceased`) `plus months` 36) `is before` (f's `the day of the death`))
    THEN `the earlier of` (f's `the day the claim became discoverable by the deceased`) `and` `the plaintiff's day`
    ELSE `the plaintiff's day`
    WHERE
        `the plaintiff's day` MEANS
            IF (f's `the day the claim became discoverable by the plaintiff`) `is on or before` (f's `the day the personal representative was appointed`)
            THEN f's `the day the personal representative was appointed`
            ELSE f's `the day the claim became discoverable by the plaintiff`

-- s 50E(1)(a): discoverable "when the victim turns 25 years of age or when the cause of action is actually
-- discoverable by the victim, whichever is the later"; (b) the long-stop runs "from when the victim turns 25".
-- s 50E(3): if the victim dies before 25, for a survivor action the references to turning 25 are to the death. For a
-- compensation to relatives action s 50E has no such rule: the day the victim would have turned 25 is taken (fork F5).
GIVEN f IS A `Claim facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the s 50E day for` f MEANS
    IF     f's `the plaintiff` EQUALS `the personal representative of the injured person, who has died, suing for the estate (a survivor action)`
       AND ((f's `the day of the death`) `is before` (`the 25th birthday after` (f's `the injured person's date of birth`)))
    THEN f's `the day of the death`
    ELSE `the 25th birthday after` (f's `the injured person's date of birth`)

GIVEN f IS A `Claim facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the claim is discoverable for` f MEANS
    IF `s 50E applies to` f
    THEN `the later of` (`the s 50E day for` f) `and` `the day before s 50E`
    ELSE `the day before s 50E`
    WHERE
        `the day before s 50E` MEANS
            CONSIDER f's `the plaintiff`
            WHEN `relatives suing for the death (a compensation to relatives action)` THEN `the later of` (f's `the day the claim became discoverable by the plaintiff`) `and` (f's `the day of the death`)
            WHEN `the personal representative of the injured person, who has died, suing for the estate (a survivor action)` THEN `the s 50C(2) day for` f
            OTHERWISE f's `the day the claim became discoverable by the plaintiff`

-- s 50C(1)(b): the long-stop runs "from the time of the act or omission"; s 50C(3): for a compensation to relatives
-- action "from the death of the deceased"; s 50E(1)(b): from the 25th birthday (fork F5: s 50E prevails over s 50C(3)).
GIVEN f IS A `Claim facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the long-stop runs from for` f MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 50E applies to` f
        THEN `the s 50E day for` f
        IF f's `the plaintiff` EQUALS `relatives suing for the death (a compensation to relatives action)`
        THEN f's `the day of the death`
        OTHERWISE f's `the day of the act or omission`

§§ `Disability (s 50F for Division 6, s 52 otherwise), fraud (s 55) and the ultimate bar (s 51)`

DECLARE `Period end` IS ONE OF
    `ends on` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `stopped while the incapacity continues, and ends at the latest on` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE

-- s 55(1): where the claim is based on fraud or deceit, or it or the defendant's identity is fraudulently concealed,
-- the time after the period starts and before the person "first discovers, or may with reasonable diligence discover"
-- it "does not count" against "a person answerable for the fraud deceit or concealment" (s 55(3): a party to it or a
-- successor). So the period counts from the later of its start and that day. s 50F(5) does not exclude s 55 from
-- Division 6.
GIVEN f IS A `Claim facts`, `the day the period starts` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day counting starts for` f `from` `the day the period starts` MEANS
    IF f's `there was fraud, deceit or concealment by the defendant`
    THEN `the later of` `the day the period starts` `and` (f's `the day the fraud or concealment was or could have been discovered`)
    ELSE `the day the period starts`

-- Disability. Outside Division 6, s 11(3): a person is under a disability "(a) while the person is under the age of
-- eighteen years, or (b) while the person is, for a continuous period of twenty-eight days or upwards, incapable of, or
-- substantially impeded in, the management of his or her affairs in relation to the cause of action". s 52(1): the
-- running of the period "is suspended for the duration of the disability", and if it "would expire before the lapse of
-- three years after" the person last ceases to be under a disability, it "is extended so as to expire three years
-- after" that day. In Division 6, s 50F(1), (2): suspended while the person "(a) is a minor, but not while the minor
-- has a capable parent or guardian, or (b) is an incapacitated person for a continuous period of 28 days or more, but
-- not while the person is a protected person"; no three-year extension (s 50F(5) excludes s 52). Only the injured
-- person's own disability is counted, and only where that person sues (fork F6); one spell of incapacity (fork F7).
GIVEN f IS A `Claim facts`, `under Division 6` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day counting starts` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `minority counts for` f `in Division 6` `under Division 6` `from` `the day counting starts` IF
        f's `the plaintiff` EQUALS `the person injured or wronged, suing for themselves`
    AND (`the day counting starts` `is before` (`the 18th birthday after` (f's `the injured person's date of birth`)))
    AND (    (NOT `under Division 6`)
          OR (NOT (f's `the injured person had a capable parent or guardian while a minor`)))

GIVEN f IS A `Claim facts`, `under Division 6` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `incapacity counts for` f `in Division 6` `under Division 6` IF
        f's `the plaintiff` EQUALS `the person injured or wronged, suing for themselves`
    AND f's `the injured person was incapacitated`
    AND (    (NOT (f's `the incapacity has ended`))
          OR ((`the days from` (f's `the day the incapacity began`) `to` (f's `the day the incapacity ended`)) AT LEAST 28))
    AND (    (NOT `under Division 6`)
          OR (NOT (f's `the injured person was a protected person while incapacitated`)))

-- The end of one period. `the day it runs from` is the day the Part 2 period runs from (s 51 counts 30 years from it);
-- `the unsuspended last day` already allows for s 55.
GIVEN f IS A `Claim facts`
      `under Division 6` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it runs from` IS A DATE
      `the day counting starts` IS A DATE
      `the unsuspended last day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Period end`
`the end of the period for` f `in Division 6` `under Division 6` `running from` `the day it runs from` `counting from` `the day counting starts` `with last day` `the unsuspended last day` MEANS
    IF `the incapacity is still stopping the clock`
    THEN `stopped while the incapacity continues, and ends at the latest on` `the 30-year day`
    ELSE `ends on` (`the earlier of` `the last day after s 52(1)(e)` `and` `the 30-year day`)
    WHERE
        `the 30-year day` MEANS `the day it runs from` `plus months` 360
        `the minority counts` MEANS `minority counts for` f `in Division 6` `under Division 6` `from` `the day counting starts`
        `the 18th birthday` MEANS `the 18th birthday after` (f's `the injured person's date of birth`)
        `the last day after minority` MEANS
            IF `the minority counts`
            THEN `the unsuspended last day` `plus days` (`the days from` `the day counting starts` `to` `the 18th birthday`)
            ELSE `the unsuspended last day`
        `the day the counted incapacity begins` MEANS
            IF `the minority counts`
            THEN `the later of` (f's `the day the incapacity began`) `and` (`the later of` `the day counting starts` `and` `the 18th birthday`)
            ELSE `the later of` (f's `the day the incapacity began`) `and` `the day counting starts`
        `the incapacity counts in time` MEANS
                `incapacity counts for` f `in Division 6` `under Division 6`
            AND (`the day the counted incapacity begins` `is on or before` `the last day after minority`)
        `the incapacity is still stopping the clock` MEANS
                `the incapacity counts in time`
            AND (NOT (f's `the incapacity has ended`))
        `the last day after incapacity` MEANS
            IF     `the incapacity counts in time`
               AND (`the day the counted incapacity begins` `is before` (f's `the day the incapacity ended`))
            THEN `the last day after minority` `plus days` (`the days from` `the day the counted incapacity begins` `to` (f's `the day the incapacity ended`))
            ELSE `the last day after minority`
        `the last day the disability ceased` MEANS
            IF     `the incapacity counts in time`
               AND (`the day the counted incapacity begins` `is before` (f's `the day the incapacity ended`))
            THEN f's `the day the incapacity ended`
            ELSE `the 18th birthday`
        `some disability counted` MEANS
                `the minority counts`
            OR (    `the incapacity counts in time`
                AND (`the day the counted incapacity begins` `is before` (f's `the day the incapacity ended`)))
        `the last day after s 52(1)(e)` MEANS
            IF (NOT `under Division 6`) AND `some disability counted`
            THEN `the later of` `the last day after incapacity` `and` (`the last day the disability ceased` `plus months` 36)
            ELSE `the last day after incapacity`

-- s 50C(1)(a): "the 3 year post discoverability limitation period, which is the period of 3 years running from and
-- including the date on which the cause of action is discoverable" (fork F2: the last day is the day before the third
-- anniversary).
GIVEN f IS A `Claim facts`
GIVETH A `Period end`
`the 3-year post-discoverability period end for` f MEANS
    `the end of the period for` f `in Division 6` TRUE `running from` `the discoverable day` `counting from` `the counting day` `with last day` ((`the counting day` `plus months` 36) `plus days` (0 MINUS 1))
    WHERE
        `the discoverable day` MEANS `the day the claim is discoverable for` f
        `the counting day` MEANS `the day counting starts for` f `from` `the discoverable day`

-- s 50C(1)(b): "the 12 year long-stop limitation period, which is the period of 12 years running from the time of the
-- act or omission".
GIVEN f IS A `Claim facts`
GIVETH A `Period end`
`the 12-year long-stop period end for` f MEANS
    `the end of the period for` f `in Division 6` TRUE `running from` `the long-stop day` `counting from` `the counting day` `with last day` (`the counting day` `plus months` 144)
    WHERE
        `the long-stop day` MEANS `the day the long-stop runs from for` f
        `the counting day` MEANS `the day counting starts for` f `from` `the long-stop day`

GIVEN `the period end` IS A `Period end`
GIVETH A DATE
`the day of` `the period end` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the period end`
    WHEN `ends on` d THEN d
    WHEN `stopped while the incapacity continues, and ends at the latest on` d THEN d

GIVEN `the period end` IS A `Period end`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is stopped` `the period end` IF
    CONSIDER `the period end`
    WHEN `stopped while the incapacity continues, and ends at the latest on` d THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 50C(1): "whichever of the following periods is the first to expire". A period stopped by a continuing incapacity
-- has not expired; it can expire no later than its s 51 day.
GIVEN `the first` IS A `Period end`, `the second` IS A `Period end`
GIVETH A `Period end`
`the first to expire of` `the first` `and` `the second` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`is stopped` `the first`) AND (`is stopped` `the second`)
        THEN `stopped while the incapacity continues, and ends at the latest on` (`the earlier of` (`the day of` `the first`) `and` (`the day of` `the second`))
        IF `is stopped` `the first`
        THEN IF (`the day of` `the second`) `is on or before` (`the day of` `the first`)
             THEN `the second`
             ELSE `the first`
        IF `is stopped` `the second`
        THEN IF (`the day of` `the first`) `is on or before` (`the day of` `the second`)
             THEN `the first`
             ELSE `the second`
        OTHERWISE `ends on` (`the earlier of` (`the day of` `the first`) `and` (`the day of` `the second`))

§§ `The last day`

DECLARE `Last day answer` IS ONE OF
    `the last day to commence the action is` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `the time is stopped while your incapacity continues (s 50F, s 52), but the action is barred after` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `there is no last day: an action for child abuse may be brought at any time (s 6A)`
    `this Act does not fix the time: another Act fixes the limitation period (s 7(a))`
    `not covered by this encoding`

GIVEN `the period end` IS A `Period end`
GIVETH A `Last day answer`
`the last day answer from` `the period end` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the period end`
    WHEN `ends on` d THEN `the last day to commence the action is` d
    WHEN `stopped while the incapacity continues, and ends at the latest on` d THEN `the time is stopped while your incapacity continues (s 50F, s 52), but the action is barred after` d

-- The periods outside Division 6, with s 55 and s 52, and s 51. s 52(3): s 52 does not apply to a penalty or
-- forfeiture (except for an aggrieved party, fork F8).
GIVEN f IS A `Claim facts`
GIVETH A `Period end`
`the ordinary period end for` f MEANS
    IF `the period for` f EQUALS `2 years running from the day the cause of action accrued (s 18)`
    THEN `ends on` (`the earlier of` (`the counting day` `plus months` 24) `and` (`the start` `plus months` 360))
    ELSE `the end of the period for` f `in Division 6` FALSE `running from` `the start` `counting from` `the counting day` `with last day` (`the counting day` `plus months` (`the months in` (`the period for` f)))
    WHERE
        `the start` MEANS `the day the ordinary period runs from for` f
        `the counting day` MEANS `the day counting starts for` f `from` `the start`

GIVEN f IS A `Claim facts`
GIVETH A `Last day answer`
`the last day for` f MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the period for` f EQUALS `none: an action for child abuse may be brought at any time (s 6A)`
        THEN `there is no last day: an action for child abuse may be brought at any time (s 6A)`
        IF `the period for` f EQUALS `no: nothing in this Act applies where another Act fixes the limitation period (s 7(a); for a motor accident claim also s 50A(3))`
        THEN `this Act does not fix the time: another Act fixes the limitation period (s 7(a))`
        IF     `the period for` f EQUALS `not covered: a kind of claim this encoding does not cover`
            OR `the period for` f EQUALS `not covered: a personal injury claim that accrued before 1 September 1990 (Part 3 Division 3 Subdivision 1)`
        THEN `not covered by this encoding`
        IF `Division 6 applies to` f
        THEN `the last day answer from` (`the first to expire of` (`the 3-year post-discoverability period end for` f) `and` (`the 12-year long-stop period end for` f))
        OTHERWISE `the last day answer from` (`the ordinary period end for` f)

§§ `Discoverability (s 50D), as a question of its own`

DECLARE `Discoverable answer` IS ONE OF
    `your claim counts as discoverable from` HAS `the day` IS A DATE
    `s 50D does not reach this: discoverability sets the time only for a personal injury claim under Division 6`

GIVEN f IS A `Claim facts`
GIVETH A `Discoverable answer`
`the discoverable answer for` f MEANS
    IF `Division 6 applies to` f
    THEN `your claim counts as discoverable from` (`the day the claim is discoverable for` f)
    ELSE `s 50D does not reach this: discoverability sets the time only for a personal injury claim under Division 6`

§§ `Part 3 Division 4 -- the court's extensions for a Division 6 claim`

-- s 62A(1), (2): a person with a Division 6 claim "may apply to a court for the extension of the 12 year long-stop
-- limitation period"; the court "may, if it decides that it is just and reasonable to do so, order the extension ...
-- for such period as the court determines, but not so as to extend that period beyond the period of 3 years after the
-- date on which the cause of action is discoverable". s 62F: the application and order may be made after the period
-- has expired. The 3-year post-discoverability period still bars the action (s 50C(1)), and s 51 is not displaced
-- (s 51(2) excepts only Division 3 Subdivision 3 orders), so the latest day is the earliest of the three (finding 3).
DECLARE `Long-stop extension answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes, if the court decides it is just and reasonable: the court may extend the 12-year long-stop, and the last day you could then commence is` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `not on these facts: the court may extend only if it decides that it is just and reasonable to do so (s 62A(2))`
    `no help: the 3-year post-discoverability period ends no later than the long-stop, and s 62A extends only the long-stop`
    `s 62A does not reach this: it extends only the 12-year long-stop of a personal injury claim under Division 6`

GIVEN f IS A `Claim facts`, `the court decides it is just and reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Long-stop extension answer`
`the s 62A answer for` f `if just and reasonable` `the court decides it is just and reasonable` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Division 6 applies to` f)
        THEN `s 62A does not reach this: it extends only the 12-year long-stop of a personal injury claim under Division 6`
        IF (`the day of` `the 3-year end`) `is on or before` (`the day of` `the long-stop end`)
        THEN `no help: the 3-year post-discoverability period ends no later than the long-stop, and s 62A extends only the long-stop`
        IF NOT `the court decides it is just and reasonable`
        THEN `not on these facts: the court may extend only if it decides that it is just and reasonable to do so (s 62A(2))`
        OTHERWISE `yes, if the court decides it is just and reasonable: the court may extend the 12-year long-stop, and the last day you could then commence is` (`the earlier of` (`the earlier of` ((`the day the claim is discoverable for` f) `plus months` 36) `and` (`the day of` `the 3-year end`)) `and` ((`the day the long-stop runs from for` f) `plus months` 360))
    WHERE
        `the 3-year end` MEANS `the 3-year post-discoverability period end for` f
        `the long-stop end` MEANS `the 12-year long-stop period end for` f

-- s 62D(1), (2): a person "who was a minor at the time of the act or omission" may apply; if "(a) the limitation period
-- applicable to the cause of action expired before or within 1 year after the applicant reached 18 years of age, and
-- (b) the failure to bring an action ... within that limitation period is attributable to an irrational decision by a
-- parent or guardian of the applicant made while the applicant was a minor, and (c) there is evidence to establish the
-- cause of action, apart from any defence founded on the expiration of a limitation period, the court may order that
-- the limitation period ... be extended so that it expires at the end of one year after the making of the court's
-- order." (b) and (c) are the court's findings: inputs.
DECLARE `Minor's extension answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes, if the court so orders: the limitation period may be extended to expire one year after the court's order (s 62D(2))`
    `not on these facts: the court may extend only if your parent's or guardian's irrational decision, made while you were a minor, caused the failure to sue, and there is evidence to establish the claim (s 62D(2)(b), (c))`
    `no: s 62D is only for a person who was a minor at the time of the act or omission (s 62D(1))`
    `no: s 62D reaches only a limitation period that expired before, or within 1 year after, you turned 18 (s 62D(2)(a))`
    `s 62D does not reach this: it is for the injured person's own claim under Division 6`

GIVEN f IS A `Claim facts`
      `the failure was attributable to an irrational decision of a parent or guardian` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to establish the cause of action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Minor's extension answer`
`the s 62D answer for` f `irrational decision` `the failure was attributable to an irrational decision of a parent or guardian` `evidence` `there is evidence to establish the cause of action` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF    (NOT (`Division 6 applies to` f))
           OR (NOT (f's `the plaintiff` EQUALS `the person injured or wronged, suing for themselves`))
        THEN `s 62D does not reach this: it is for the injured person's own claim under Division 6`
        IF NOT ((f's `the day of the act or omission`) `is before` `the 18th birthday`)
        THEN `no: s 62D is only for a person who was a minor at the time of the act or omission (s 62D(1))`
        IF    (`is stopped` `the period end`)
           OR (NOT ((`the day of` `the period end`) `is on or before` (`the 18th birthday` `plus months` 12)))
        THEN `no: s 62D reaches only a limitation period that expired before, or within 1 year after, you turned 18 (s 62D(2)(a))`
        IF     `the failure was attributable to an irrational decision of a parent or guardian`
           AND `there is evidence to establish the cause of action`
        THEN `yes, if the court so orders: the limitation period may be extended to expire one year after the court's order (s 62D(2))`
        OTHERWISE `not on these facts: the court may extend only if your parent's or guardian's irrational decision, made while you were a minor, caused the failure to sue, and there is evidence to establish the claim (s 62D(2)(b), (c))`
    WHERE
        `the 18th birthday` MEANS `the 18th birthday after` (f's `the injured person's date of birth`)
        `the period end` MEANS `the first to expire of` (`the 3-year post-discoverability period end for` f) `and` (`the 12-year long-stop period end for` f)

§§ `Part 4 Division 1 -- what expiry does to the right (s 63)`

-- s 63(1): "on the expiration of a limitation period fixed by or under this Act for a cause of action to recover any
-- debt damages or other money, the right and title of the person formerly having the cause of action to the debt
-- damages or other money is, as against the person against whom the cause of action formerly lay and as against the
-- person's successors, extinguished." s 63(2): not where an action was brought before expiry. s 62F(1), (3): a
-- Division 4 order may be made "as if Division 1 of Part 4 had never been in force", and an expiry so extended "has no
-- effect".
DECLARE `Expiry answer` IS ONE OF
    `nothing expires: there is no limitation period for an action for child abuse (s 6A)`
    `when the period expires your right to the damages is extinguished as against the defendant and their successors, unless you brought your action before then (s 63(1), (2)); a court may still extend the period under Part 3 Division 4, and the expiry then has no effect (s 62F)`
    `when the period expires your right to the money is extinguished as against the defendant and their successors, unless you brought your action before then (s 63(1), (2))`
    `this Act does not say what happens: another Act fixes the limitation period (s 7(a))`
    `not covered: what happens is not worked out here for this kind of claim`

GIVEN f IS A `Claim facts`
GIVETH A `Expiry answer`
`the expiry answer for` f MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day for` f
    WHEN `there is no last day: an action for child abuse may be brought at any time (s 6A)` THEN `nothing expires: there is no limitation period for an action for child abuse (s 6A)`
    WHEN `this Act does not fix the time: another Act fixes the limitation period (s 7(a))` THEN `this Act does not say what happens: another Act fixes the limitation period (s 7(a))`
    WHEN `not covered by this encoding` THEN `not covered: what happens is not worked out here for this kind of claim`
    OTHERWISE
        IF `Division 6 applies to` f
        THEN `when the period expires your right to the damages is extinguished as against the defendant and their successors, unless you brought your action before then (s 63(1), (2)); a court may still extend the period under Part 3 Division 4, and the expiry then has no effect (s 62F)`
        ELSE `when the period expires your right to the money is extinguished as against the defendant and their successors, unless you brought your action before then (s 63(1), (2))`

§§ `Bringing the action within the period, as a regulative rule`

DECLARE `Limitation party` IS ONE OF `the plaintiff`

DECLARE `Limitation act` IS ONE OF `bring the action`

-- ss 14, 16-19, 50C: an action "is not maintainable if brought after the expiration of a limitation period". Clock:
-- day 0 is the day of the act or omission; the days allowed run to the last day worked out above.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Limitation party` `Limitation act`
`the action must be brought within the limitation period` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY  `the plaintiff`
    MUST   `bring the action`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    LEST   BREACH BY `the plaintiff` BECAUSE "the action was brought after the limitation period fixed by the Limitation Act 1969 expired"

DECLARE `Time limit answer` IS ONE OF
    `in time: it was brought on or before the last day`
    `late: it was brought after the last day`
    `still in time: it has not been brought yet and the last day has not passed`
    `late: it has not been brought and the last day has passed`
    `in time: there is no limitation period for an action for child abuse (s 6A)`
    `this Act does not say: another Act fixes the limitation period (s 7(a))`
    `not covered: the time limit for this kind of claim is not worked out here`

-- On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH: where the action was brought,
-- FULFILLED means in time and anything else late; where it was not, the helper asks whether bringing it today would
-- still be in time. It takes a DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Limitation party` `Limitation act`
      `the clock start` IS A DATE
      `it has been brought` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it was brought` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Time limit answer`
`the deadline` `the rule` `from` `the clock start` `brought` `it has been brought` `on` `the day it was brought` `as of` `today` MEANS
    IF `it has been brought`
    THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the plaintiff` `bring the action` (`the days from` `the clock start` `to` `the day it was brought`)))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `in time: it was brought on or before the last day`
         OTHERWISE `late: it was brought after the last day`
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the plaintiff` `bring the action` (`the days from` `the clock start` `to` `today`)))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `still in time: it has not been brought yet and the last day has not passed`
         OTHERWISE `late: it has not been brought and the last day has passed`

GIVEN f IS A `Claim facts`, `the last day` IS A DATE, `brought` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day brought` IS A DATE, `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Time limit answer`
`the deadline for` f `ending` `the last day` `whether brought` `brought` `on` `the day brought` `as of` `today` MEANS
    `the deadline` (`the action must be brought within the limitation period` (`the days from` (f's `the day of the act or omission`) `to` `the last day`)) `from` (f's `the day of the act or omission`) `brought` `brought` `on` `the day brought` `as of` `today`

GIVEN f IS A `Claim facts`, `brought` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day brought` IS A DATE, `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Time limit answer`
`was the action brought in time` f `brought` `the day brought` `today` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day for` f
    WHEN `the last day to commence the action is` d THEN `the deadline for` f `ending` d `whether brought` `brought` `on` `the day brought` `as of` `today`
    WHEN `the time is stopped while your incapacity continues (s 50F, s 52), but the action is barred after` d THEN `the deadline for` f `ending` d `whether brought` `brought` `on` `the day brought` `as of` `today`
    WHEN `there is no last day: an action for child abuse may be brought at any time (s 6A)` THEN `in time: there is no limitation period for an action for child abuse (s 6A)`
    WHEN `this Act does not fix the time: another Act fixes the limitation period (s 7(a))` THEN `this Act does not say: another Act fixes the limitation period (s 7(a))`
    OTHERWISE `not covered: the time limit for this kind of claim is not worked out here`
